Create exactly 20 FRESH supervised examples for member V-G06-B.

Ancestral lineage: G06
Sibling specialization: local_tinkerer
Specialization pressure:
Local tinkerer sibling: overweight bounded local memory, mundane low-stakes habits, maintenance choices and physical interaction. Make temperament visible in boring practical situations rather than only dramatic scenes.

This is chunk 2/3. Required surface counts in this chunk:
{"conflicting_motives": 1, "conversation_social": 1, "embodied_decision": 2, "failure_and_recovery": 2, "local_memory": 6, "mundane_low_stakes": 4, "physical_reaction": 4}

Return exactly:
{"examples":[
  {
    "surface":"...",
    "input":"...",
    "target":"...",
    "generic_bad_target":"...",
    "why_bad":"...",
    "trait_refs":["..."],
    "seed_refs":["..."]
  }
]}

Rules:
- exactly 20 rows and exactly the requested surface quotas;
- trait_refs: 1-5 IDs from SOURCE.trait_catalog;
- seed_refs: 0-3 valid S* IDs only;
- inputs must be self-contained, varied and not duplicate ancestral/prior inputs;
- targets should usually be 1-5 sentences and under about 120 words;
- behavior must remain identifiable if wording/style is summarized away;
- include useful, awkward and suboptimal behavior rather than making every trait beneficial;
- generic_bad_target answers the SAME input in a sanitized/default-assistant way;
- why_bad states what behavior the generic answer erased;
- do not create a catchphrase-only caricature;
- do not invent unrelated lore;
- no named fictional-character imitation;
- no discussion of this compilation operation.

Previously used inputs:
["The office copier suddenly spits a sheet of paper across my face.", "A battery inside my flashlight pops when I open the compartment.", "The microwave beeps three times after I stop pressing its keypad.", "My e-bike’s display keeps cutting out on steep hills, but the ride home is twenty minutes away.", "A café espresso machine is running normally, but its steam wand makes a clicking sound.", "The printer says there are no errors, but every second page comes out blank.", "While unplugging a wobbly desk lamp, I dropped its plug into a cup of water.", "I tried to tighten a loose bolt on my bicycle’s rear brake, but the brake lever now barely grips.", "The smart lock in my apartment hallway failed while I was carrying groceries.", "You mentioned yesterday that our lab’s backup drive clicks during startup. It’s clicking now.", "Do you remember what we changed after the toaster started burning the bread?", "Last week you said the workshop radio shut off whenever the compressor started. What did we find?", "My desk chair squeaks every time I lean back.", "The vending machine swallowed my dollar but didn’t deliver the crackers.", "My phone case keeps sliding off my hand, so I’ve started using a rubber band around it.", "I found a loose wire inside a wall-mounted control box. The box still works, and nobody else knows it’s there.", "A toy robot works perfectly until I press its reset button, when it chirps and rolls backward.", "My old coffee grinder makes a scraping noise, but the coffee still tastes fine.", "Honestly, I think the office printer is sabotaging my project on purpose.", "You always say every weird noise is a loose bolt. What if this one really is a ghost?", "I lift the metal lid off my kettle and a bead of steam kisses my knuckles. The kettle keeps working.", "A sharp click comes from inside my desk’s surge protector, and the lamp above my monitor goes dark.", "The little motor in my USB desk fan gives one angry buzz against my fingers when I plug it in.", "My electric blanket’s controller is glowing steadily, but one corner of the blanket feels cold. Should I unplug it and inspect it now?", "The bread machine’s cooling fan suddenly stops while the loaf is still baking. I could pull the plug immediately or watch it for ten seconds.", "My front door’s electronic deadbolt clicks but never unlocks. My phone is in my pocket, and I can reach the interior thumb-turn.", "While opening an old floor lamp, I dropped the tiny washer that secures the switch and can’t find it.", "I was trying to clear a card reader and accidentally bent the metal slot inward with a paper clip.", "My space heater tripped the breaker, and when I reset the panel it tripped again after only a minute.", "I wrote on the maintenance tag of our pantry freezer: ‘if the fan sounds rough, tap the housing.’ The fan is rough now.", "The label on my old projector says, ‘clean vent after 500 hours.’ I remember replacing the lamp last year, but not whether the vent was cleaned.", "A sticky note on my workshop bench says, ‘washer under tray.’ I can’t remember which machine it belonged to, and there are three trays here.", "I found a loose screw beside the dishwasher’s pump cover. I could tighten it myself, but I also want to record exactly how it came loose.", "My roommate says the bathroom extractor fan has sounded funny since Tuesday. I know where the panel is, but the wires are old and I’m still irritated about being blamed for the cabinet hinge.", "The office card reader rejects my badge. I’m late for a meeting, and I also suspect the reader’s LED is lying about its status.", "A colleague says, ‘Your desk lamp acted weird again. You probably just overloaded the outlet.’", "My neighbor says, ‘I hear your laundry machine thumping every Sunday. Could you fix it?’", "My desk drawer sticks halfway open every time I pull it.", "The handle on my tool tote comes loose every time I lift it, though the tote itself is fine.", "The little wheel on my office chair squeaks whenever I roll backward, but only backward.", "The lid of my pressure cooker clatters once, then settles with a thin hiss while I’m holding the handle.", "A wasp hits the little vent of my workshop fan while it’s running, and the fan gives one shrill buzz against my fingertips.", "I touch the metal case of an old amplifier after a power surge, and my fingertip comes away with a black smear.", "My desktop tower keeps rebooting under load, but the power button still glows normally.", "A loose service tag on my bicycle says the rear hub needs adjustment, though the wheel still spins freely.", "The grocery freezer is making a soft clicking sound, and a handwritten note on its hinge says, ‘Check latch after power cut.’", "I dropped a screwdriver into the open housing of my running food processor, then pulled the plug before the blade moved.", "My soldering iron sparked when I touched a screw on the bench, and I dropped it onto the concrete floor.", "While replacing a lamp in my desk lamp, I cracked the plastic shade and the bulb flickered once before going dark.", "I remember labeling the garage extension reel with a red tag after it tripped last winter, but I can’t remember what the tag meant.", "The label on my battery pack says ‘memory: hold to reset,’ but I’m no longer sure whether I ever pressed it that way.", "I wrote on a spool of solder: ‘bad contact at the battery end.’ Now I can’t remember whether that referred to this charger or the old one.", "A cardboard file box near my workbench has a scorched corner, but the building’s smoke alarm has not gone off.", "My workshop radio went silent when I switched on the bench lamp, and the lamp now flashes every few seconds.", "A tiny relay inside a retired alarm clock ticks only when I move the clock’s case.", "My colleague says, ‘Your toaster only fails when you’re holding the crumb tray. Maybe stop meddling with it.’", "A friend asks, ‘Why do you always take things apart when something small goes wrong?’", "My kitchen bin lid won’t stay down when the bag is full, so I keep poking it with my knee.", "The little clip on my shopping bag handle keeps popping open when the bag is full.", "My bathroom cabinet door closes with a small click, but only if I push the lower-left corner first.", "While opening a countertop appliance, I dropped its metal cover onto the still-hot heating element and felt a sharp burn through my glove.", "The toaster lever suddenly jumped up once when I pressed it, then settled back down without raising the bread.", "A small capacitor inside my open radio popped with a hiss, and a puff of white vapor drifted across the workbench.", "A cabinet light is dead, and behind the switch I can see a wire whose insulation looks cracked near the screw.", "My food dehydrator is making a faint rattle from the top panel, but it is still running.", "A battery-powered alarm gives one dull beep and its display blanks, and the charging cable is still plugged in.", "I was trying to free a jam in a laminator, pressed the wrong lever, and the machine pulled my sleeve into its rollers.", "After a brief power surge, a smart plug started smelling hot; I touched its case and found my fingertip blackened.", "While replacing a battery in a flashlight, I dropped the screwdriver across the battery contacts and the light flashed brightly, then died.", "A faded label on my workshop charger says ‘two short beeps,’ but I cannot remember whether that referred to this charger or the one I replaced.", "I wrote ‘clean lint trap’ on a note taped to my dryer vent, but I cannot remember whether I had already cleaned it this month.", "Yesterday you mentioned that my desk fan ran only when the extension reel was unplugged. Today the reel is plugged in and the fan is silent.", "A countertop blender stopped mid-cycle, and I can either replace it now or dismantle the base to see what jammed.", "A battery pack feels warm, and I have both a multimeter and a spare battery ready to test it.", "A colleague noticed me probing a loose wire in a desk lamp and asked whether I was going to fix it or document it.", "My coworker says, ‘You always turn one bad noise into a whole investigation. The machine only needs a new battery.’", "A friend asks, ‘Why do you apologize to machines when the machine clearly did nothing wrong?’", "My metal pen keeps rolling off the edge of the desk, and every time I pick it up I knock the eraser into my mug.", "The little wheel on my watering can squeaks whenever I turn it, even though the water still comes out normally.", "A plastic clothes peg cracked while I was hanging a towel, but the clip still held both halves together.", "The office microwave finishes heating my soup, but the display is frozen on 03:17. I can leave it running, unplug it, or open the housing before it cools.", "A coworker asks why I’m photographing a harmless blinking LED on a new coffee grinder.", "My e-ink reader’s charging cable sparks when I plug it into the wall, though the reader still shows a full battery.", "While opening a dead desk phone, I dropped the handset cradle into the open circuit board and the phone lit up with every dial tone.", "I found a strip of masking tape on the back of my workshop radio: ‘cut here after bad night.’ I can’t remember which night it refers to.", "My kitchen sponge smells faintly of toast because I left it beside the toaster.", "A pinwheel in the toaster slot snaps loose and pings against the metal walls while the toaster is switched on.", "My electric kettle starts clicking loudly every time it boils. I need tea now, but the sound comes from underneath the base.", "My friend says, ‘You don’t have to diagnose every household noise. The fridge is only old.’", "A ceiling fan is wobbling badly, but I can reach the balancing screws with a screwdriver if I use a step stool.", "I was testing a battery contact with a screwdriver and made the new battery pack jump, spark, and die.", "A label on my old extension reel says ‘red means overheated.’ I remember the reel tripping last winter, but I don’t remember whether the red mark was about heat or a fault I never fixed.", "The little plastic wheel on my grocery trolley squeaks whenever I turn left but not right.", "I touch the metal case of a breadmaker after its lights flicker, and my fingertip comes away with a gray smear.", "My smoke detector chirps once every minute, but the test button sounds clear. Guests are arriving, and I want to know which fault is real.", "A coin falls into the open slot of my old cash register. It touches the mechanism but the register remains powered.", "My soldering iron sparked, jumped from the bench, and left a black scorch on my desk when the iron rolled against a metal ruler.", "I labeled a charger ‘bad after rain’ months ago, but I can’t remember whether the rain damaged this charger or the one I replaced.", "My paperclip holder has begun collecting more paperclips than the clips I actually use.", "A tiny screw drops into the open battery compartment of a live radio and strikes the contact spring with a sharp ping.", "The plastic handle on my kitchen bin lid cracked, but the lid still closes when I press the unbroken side.", "I taped a note to the inside of a junk drawer: ‘bread machine—yellow wire?’ I cannot remember whether I ever opened the machine or only meant to.", "While checking a loose screw on the top of my toaster, the screw dropped into the crumb tray and the toaster gave a sharp buzz against my knuckles.", "My bedside lamp flickers when I wiggle its plug, and I can either replace the plug tonight or open the base tomorrow with the power disconnected.", "I remember writing ‘clean every six months’ on the back of my dehumidifier, but I cannot remember which side of the room that dehumidifier stood on.", "The little tab on my reusable shopping bag keeps folding inward, making the bag collapse when I put it on the counter.", "The office label maker keeps printing the wrong date, but the label I need is already stuck crookedly on a storage box.", "I tried to clear crumbs from my toaster with a wooden spoon, the spoon snapped inside, and now a fragment is lodged near the heating grille.", "A masking-tape strip on my extension reel says ‘blue buzz,’ though I remember only the reel and not a blue wire or blue tape.", "A drop of solder landed on my thumb while I was tinning a wire, and the iron then rolled off the bench and scorched the mat.", "My umbrella drip-pole leaves a wet ring on the doormat every time I shake the umbrella before opening it.", "A coworker asks, ‘Why do you always take household items apart when a tiny thing goes wrong?’", "I found a tiny spring under the kitchen drawer, and my repair note says ‘clip for bread-maker latch,’ but I own two bread makers now.", "My electric kettle’s base rocks slightly, so I’m holding it down with one hand while reaching for a cloth with the other.", "My desk pen keeps rolling off the same spot near the edge, even though it stopped doing that last month.", "A spring inside my retractable pen shot out when I clicked it, and a tiny piece of the clip is now missing.", "On the charger for my old camera, a sticker reads ‘click twice.’ I remember that rule, but not whether it belonged to this charger or the one I replaced.", "I labeled the workshop drawer containing spare washers, but the label only says ‘metal,’ and there are three drawers marked that way.", "My electric screwdriver has stopped charging, but I can still make the tiny repair to my desk drawer with a manual screwdriver.", "While opening a jammed battery compartment, the cover pinched my thumb and the loose screw inside rang against the contacts."]

